  "live_records": {
    "q-6275": {
      "dom_id": "step-q6275",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $4x+2\\le 10.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+2 & \\le 10 \\\\ 4x+2-2 & \\le 10-2 \\\\ 4x+0 & \\le 8 \\\\ 4x & \\le 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & \\le 8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & \\le \\frac{8}{4} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{4}x}{\\cancel{4}} & \\le 2 \\\\ x & \\le 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le 2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
