    "q-177680": {
      "dom_id": "step-q177680",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The solution to the inequality $-7t+2\\le -5$ is $t${{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $2$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7t+2 & \\le -5 \\\\ -7t+2-2 & \\le -5-2 \\\\ -7t+0 & \\le -7 \\\\ -7t & \\le -7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-7.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7t\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-7 \\\\ \\frac{-7t}{-7}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-7}{-7} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-7}t}{\\cancel{-7}}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,1 \\\\ t\\,\\, & \\ge \\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t\\ge 1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
