    "q-177679": {
      "dom_id": "step-q177679",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "The solution to the inequality $-5y+16\\le -4$ is $y${{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $16$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y+16 & \\le -4 \\\\ -5y+16-16 & \\le -4-16 \\\\ -5y+0 & \\le -20 \\\\ -5y & \\le -20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-5.$ \n\nRemember, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5y\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-20 \\\\ \\frac{-5y}{-5}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-20}{-5} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-5}y}{\\cancel{-5}}\\, & \\ge \\,\\,4 \\\\ y\\,\\, & \\ge \\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y\\ge 4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
