    "q-154276": {
      "dom_id": "step-q154276",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Solve the inequality $-1\\le 5x+14.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $14$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\le 5x+14 \\\\ -1-14 & \\le 5x+14-14 \\\\ -15 & \\le 5x+0 \\\\ -15 & \\le 5x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-15 & \\le 5x \\\\ -\\frac{15}{5} & \\le \\frac{5x}{5} \\\\ -3 & \\le \\frac{\\cancel{5}x}{\\cancel{5}} \\\\ -3 & \\le x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side. Remember, we also need to flip the inequality.\n\n$$\nx\\ge -3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
